  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the most critical uncertainty is establishing a reliable baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most interpretable configuration: a single modality with a standard linear encoder and no aggregation or fusion complexity. It isolates the raw RNA signal and provides a reference performance against which every subsequent design choice (alternative encoders, multiprofile aggregation, image modality, fusion strategy) can be meaningfully compared. Starting here minimizes confounding, is computationally cheap, and if it performs poorly, immediately flags a data-quality or task-difficulty issue before investing in more complex configurations. This is the highest-information first experiment under a limited budget."
